---
import Since from '../../components/Since.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/Snippet.astro';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';

const hierarchy = `ZvukError                       extends Error
├─ EngineClosedError            the engine was closed
├─ BusNotFoundError             a bus name nobody declared
├─ SoundNotFoundError           a sound, sprite, variant set, music or stream name
├─ SpriteRegionNotFoundError    a region the sprite doesn't have      .sprite .region   (v2)
├─ DecodeError                  one URL failed to fetch or decode
│  └─ AggregateDecodeError      every URL in a codec ladder failed   .attempts
└─ PreloadError                 one or more preload items failed     .failures`;

const narrow = `import {
  AggregateDecodeError,
  SpriteRegionNotFoundError,
  BusNotFoundError,
  DecodeError,
  PreloadError,
  ZvukError,
} from '@schmooky/zvuk';

try {
  await engine.loadSound('coin', ['/sfx/coin.webm', '/sfx/coin.m4a'], { bus: 'sfx' });
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof AggregateDecodeError) {
    for (const { url, cause } of e.attempts) console.warn(url, cause);
  } else if (e instanceof DecodeError) {
    console.warn('one URL, and it failed:', e.cause);
  } else if (e instanceof BusNotFoundError) {
    throw e; // a typo in code, not a runtime condition
  } else if ((e as Error).name === 'AbortError') {
    // the signal you passed fired; nothing to report
  } else {
    throw e;
  }
}`;

const preload = `try {
  await engine.preload(manifest, { concurrency: 4, onProgress });
} catch (e) {
  if (!(e instanceof PreloadError)) throw e;
  // Everything else in the batch loaded. Decide per item.
  for (const { name, cause } of e.failures) {
    report(name, cause);
  }
}`;

const typo = `engine.bus('sxf');
// BusNotFoundError: Bus "sxf" is not configured.
// Declare it in createEngine({ buses: { ... } }). Did you mean "sfx"?`;

const cause = `catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof ZvukError) {
    logger.error(e.message, { name: e.name, cause: e.cause });
  }
}`;
---
<Docs
  title="Errors"
  description="Which engine call throws which error class, what the message carries, and which ones are worth catching at runtime."
  eyebrow="Guide"
>
  <p>
    A loading screen that dies on the first missing file is worse than one
    that shows a gap, and a typo in a bus name should fail loudly in
    development instead of playing nothing in production. Telling those apart
    needs typed errors.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every error zvuk throws on purpose extends <a href="/api/ZvukError/"><code>ZvukError</code></a>,
    so one <code>instanceof</code> separates them from everything else. The
    original failure is kept on <code>cause</code> (since 1.14), so a logger
    that walks the cause chain still gets the network or decoder stack.
  </p>

  <h2>The classes</h2>
  <Snippet code={hierarchy} lang="plaintext" title="Hierarchy" hideBadge />

  <h2>What throws what</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Call</th><th>Throws</th><th>When</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>engine.bus(name)</code></td>
        <td><code>BusNotFoundError</code></td>
        <td>The name isn't in <code>createEngine({'{'} buses {'}'})</code>. The message suggests the closest declared name.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>engine.busGroup(name)</code></td>
        <td><code>BusNotFoundError</code></td>
        <td>Looking up a group that was never created with members.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>loadSound</code>, <code>loadSprite</code>, <code>loadVariants</code>, <code>loadMusic</code>, <code>loadStream</code>, <code>createSound</code></td>
        <td><code>BusNotFoundError</code></td>
        <td><code>options.bus</code> names an undeclared bus. Checked when the sound is registered, after the fetch.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sound.play({'{'} bus {'}'})</code>, <code>play({'{'} duck: {'{'} bus {'}'} {'}'})</code></td>
        <td><code>BusNotFoundError</code></td>
        <td>A per-play bus override, or the bus to duck, names an undeclared bus.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>engine.sound</code>, <code>sprite</code>, <code>variants</code>, <code>music</code>, <code>stream</code></td>
        <td><code>SoundNotFoundError</code></td>
        <td>Nothing is registered under that name in that registry. Each kind has its own registry, so <code>engine.sound('theme')</code> fails for a track loaded with <code>loadMusic</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>sprite.play(region)</code>, <code>sprite.region(name)</code></td>
        <td><code>SpriteRegionNotFoundError</code> <Since v="2.0" /></td>
        <td>The region isn't in the sprite map. The message lists the regions it does have; <code>sprite</code> and <code>region</code> are fields. In 1.x this was a <code>SoundNotFoundError</code> named <code>sprite#region</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>loadSprite</code></td>
        <td><code>RangeError</code> <Since v="2.0" /></td>
        <td>A region doesn't fit the decoded buffer: negative start, zero duration, or start plus duration past the end. Checked once at load, so a bad offset fails on the loading screen instead of playing silence later.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>createEngine</code> (first graph build)</td>
        <td><code>BusNotFoundError</code> <Since v="2.0" /></td>
        <td>A bus's <code>sidechain.from</code> names no bus, or names itself.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Any load with a single URL</td>
        <td><code>DecodeError</code></td>
        <td>The fetch failed, the server answered with a non-2xx status, or <code>decodeAudioData</code> rejected the bytes.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Any load with a codec ladder</td>
        <td><code>AggregateDecodeError</code></td>
        <td>Every URL failed. <code>attempts</code> holds one <code>{'{'} url, cause {'}'}</code> per URL, in the order tried.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>engine.preload(items)</code></td>
        <td><code>PreloadError</code></td>
        <td>At least one item failed. Thrown only after every item has settled; <code>failures</code> lists <code>{'{'} name, cause {'}'}</code>.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>unlock</code>, every <code>load*</code>, <code>preload</code>, <code>createSound</code>, <code>engine.context</code></td>
        <td><code>EngineClosedError</code></td>
        <td><code>close()</code> already ran. Closing is terminal; build a new engine.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    A voice refused by a concurrency or per-sound limit is not an error.
    <code>play()</code> returns a voice with <code>rejected === true</code>
    instead; see <a href="/concepts/concurrency/">Concurrency</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Things that are not a ZvukError</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An abort. When the <code>signal</code> you passed fires, the load
      rejects with the platform's <code>AbortError</code>, untouched, so the
      usual <code>e.name === 'AbortError'</code> check works.
    </li>
    <li>
      Programmer errors with no recovery, such as <code>loadVariants</code> with an
      empty URL list, <code>pickSource([])</code>, and a missing
      <code>AudioContext</code> constructor (server-side rendering, or Node
      without a polyfill). These are plain <code>Error</code>s.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Catching load failures</h2>
  <p>
    Check the subclass before the base class, since
    <code>AggregateDecodeError</code> is also a <code>DecodeError</code>.
    That ordering is deliberate, so code written before ladders existed still
    catches both.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={narrow} lang="ts" />

  <h3>A loading screen that keeps going</h3>
  <p>
    <code>preload</code> doesn't short-circuit. One bad file leaves the rest
    of the batch loaded and registered, and the rejection tells you which
    names are missing. I'd show the game and skip the missing sounds rather
    than block on them. <a href="/guides/loading/">Loading sounds</a> covers
    progress and concurrency.
  </p>
  <Snippet code={preload} lang="ts" />

  <h2>Lookup errors are for development</h2>
  <p>
    A <code>BusNotFoundError</code> or <code>SoundNotFoundError</code> at
    runtime means the code and the manifest disagree. Catching it hides the
    bug. The message names the closest match by edit distance, which is
    usually the typo:
  </p>
  <Snippet code={typo} lang="ts" />
  <p>
    If the set of sounds really is dynamic, ask first with
    <code>engine.hasSound(name)</code> (and <code>hasSprite</code>,
    <code>hasVariants</code>, <code>hasMusic</code>, <code>hasStream</code>).
    For sound names known at build time, <a href="/reference/cli/"><code>zvuk gen</code></a>
    turns the manifest into a union type so the typo never compiles.
  </p>

  <h2>Logging</h2>
  <Snippet code={cause} lang="ts" />

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/concepts/engine/">Engine</a> covers lifecycle and <code>close()</code>.</li>
    <li><a href="/guides/asset-formats/">Asset formats</a> explains the codec ladder behind <code>AggregateDecodeError</code>.</li>
    <li><a href="/api/">API reference</a> has each class.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
